{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-opposite}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27b62cf1381ed0104d6353d2986f53af6e91afb99240732aa639bb516f408c26", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7144d7ce76868586ad59e7ffe7eb57ecd8a3087c8ea13f834068774244e202cc", "source_text": "Given a category <MATH_0001> the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>opposite category<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0002> is the category with the same objects\nas <MATH_0003> but all morphisms reversed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d39357f39e859448c408a8c8f9650f8dd765209e87e6d72668d7c463eb00182", "unit_id": "tag:001M:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Mor_{\\mathcal{C}^{opp}}(x, y) = \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(y, x)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\phi : y \\to z$", "MATH_0005": "$\\psi : x \\to y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0007": "$z \\to y$", "MATH_0008": "$y \\to x$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\phi \\circ^{opp} \\psi$", "MATH_0011": "$x \\to z$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0013": "$z \\to y \\to x$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:280aceec66338cf4ed3a278a82144b1387f901f5ca8d4896b715077470b308ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9edca6e35614e686ea9a43a084c871a743131a5f3bced06f876eb2805cd705ea", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn other words\n<MATH_0001>.\nComposition in <MATH_0002> is the same as in <MATH_0003>\nexcept backwards: if <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\nare morphisms in <MATH_0006>, in other words arrows\n<MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> in <MATH_0009>,\nthen <MATH_0010> is the morphism <MATH_0011>\nof <MATH_0012> which corresponds to the composition\n<MATH_0013> in <MATH_0014>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f01476e3d08c31540a699db17e12d8d8e5a12ca63d605cf1fcdbd7ddf8e03a1b", "unit_id": "tag:001L:paragraph-0001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}\\to \\mathcal{S}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-contravariant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fed9ea42f9b2fc8cc23a9fc3e1c9e71f09b7fddf7a668c442501dc39db5820c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15e068f17bd86b301556f507fb9e347046f56b22cef7858040b96e6c8016240c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be categories.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>contravariant<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> functor <MATH_0003>\nfrom <MATH_0004> to <MATH_0005>\nis a functor <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:74be7ce233676bb5aded38425da24e23fa8171454b2e426290a4ae2043994158", "unit_id": "tag:001N:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$F : \\Ob(\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n\\Ob(\\mathcal{S})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\psi : x \\to y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$F(\\psi) : F(y) \\to F(x)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\phi : y \\to z$", "MATH_0007": "$F(\\phi \\circ \\psi)\n= F(\\psi) \\circ F(\\phi)$", "MATH_0008": "$F(z) \\to F(x)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6b2709b11638392e25a6f0f8967ad7b7006ccf82bb3e1c4dd181d5c0857ca2f5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1300c35fa494fbd0fe7e412efa7106665b0a833c17ae57d16f6a52a43849b69a", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nConcretely, a contravariant functor <MATH_0001> is given\nby a map <MATH_0002> and for every morphism\n<MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004> a morphism\n<MATH_0005>. These should satisfy the property\nthat, given another morphism\n<MATH_0006>, we have <MATH_0007> as morphisms <MATH_0008>.\n(Note the reverse of order.)", "source_text_hash": "sha256:76cf0ca407b5c894a92edb9295c7005c2a72111fd2ab698c053a99a6d8394569", "unit_id": "tag:001L:paragraph-0002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-presheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:039d552af2497279bbae8ac1f4db736f19897463f14827422a80ac5484b2bad2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e044e6dc21d708ec15dc97621ab6405b46757571eb612a6922c326db37672a31", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>presheaf of sets on <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nor simply a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is a contravariant functor\n<MATH_0003> from <MATH_0004> to <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0003> The category of presheaves is denoted <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3dd1eb523e2b80ef52957dd9b9c5d968b1226a3491af5555f0846c2d82bd1231", "unit_id": "tag:02X6:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:446023e3c53cd3eaf4931fb8bbfd60d3379fc94fa5216d884692c6e1c2d5552d", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nOf course the category of presheaves is a proper class.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d5c41c38027a288e01228ee111f664bc68a7d8f2bfea3ba2631edeec9bdfa484", "unit_id": "tag:001L:paragraph-0003"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$U\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\nh_U & : & \\mathcal{C}\n&\n\\longrightarrow\n&\n\\textit{Sets} \\\\\n& &\nX\n&\n\\longmapsto\n&\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)$", "MATH_0005": "$h_U$", "MATH_0006": "$f : X\\to Y$", "MATH_0007": "$h_U(f) : \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(Y, U)\\to \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(X, U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$\\phi\\circ f$", "MATH_0010": "$h_U : \\mathcal{C}^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0013": "$U$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-hom-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3d10b7039aed038c11d0333703e7e8de20ec703effbe7d43b1f77542503e3968", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:765f49eb63dd8e2967fab3caa6d6e34bc71fb161181c66c51d05a5c48fd2ae92", "source_text": "Functor of points.\nFor any <MATH_0001> there is a contravariant\nfunctor\n<MATH_0002>\nwhich takes an object <MATH_0003> to the set\n<MATH_0004>. In other words <MATH_0005> is a presheaf.\nGiven a morphism <MATH_0006> the corresponding map\n<MATH_0007>\ntakes <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>. We will always denote\nthis presheaf <MATH_0010>.\nIt is called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable presheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> associated to <MATH_0011>.\nIf <MATH_0012> is the category of schemes this functor is\nsometimes referred to as the\n<EMPHOPEN_0001>functor of points<EMPHCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8455fe43f49893789276a90bc518e2888be2849b6f5b1ab3b937b4ef3333ba0f", "unit_id": "tag:001O:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\nAppeared in some form in \\cite{Yoneda-homology}. Used by Grothendieck in a\ngeneralized form in \\cite{Gr-II}.\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$U, V \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$s : h_U \\to h_V$", "MATH_0003": "$\\phi : U \\to V$", "MATH_0004": "$h(\\phi) = s$", "MATH_0005": "$h$", "MATH_0006": "$F$", "MATH_0007": "$U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U, F) \\longrightarrow F(U),\n\\quad\ns \\longmapsto s_U(\\text{id}_U).\n$$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{lemma-yoneda}\n"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}[", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:db993da333ca058eebd298f6661afc328088822e613f5bd0deb7acd3205f86f0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5df5bb102791aa80362858128780ab02de84750797ccd5205c3c0ecaf547e317", "source_text": "Yoneda lemma<OWNARGEND_0001><LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001>.\nGiven any morphism of functors <MATH_0002>\nthere is a unique morphism <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004>. In other words the\nfunctor <MATH_0005> is fully faithful. More generally,\ngiven any contravariant functor <MATH_0006> and any object\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> we have a natural bijection\n<MATH_0009>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:970a92f505b4c4ebcffb554c00648442cd175f22d4d6217d3e15b504cf458468", "unit_id": "tag:001P:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\phi = s_U(\\text{id}_U) \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(U, V)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\xi \\in F(U)$", "MATH_0003": "$s$", "MATH_0004": "$s_V : h_U(V) \\to F(V)$", "MATH_0005": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$h_U(V) = \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(V, U)$", "MATH_0007": "$F(f)(\\xi)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:03c04d3638d81e98d7bcdf0435076be78c245054a3553401a061c8d9ffa425f3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:03e23660d78a8645daca255eaa052ca38962fa61902dbc221dc12fe7e54f1ed8", "source_text": "For the first statement, just take\n<MATH_0001>.\nFor the second statement, given <MATH_0002> define\n<MATH_0003> by <MATH_0004> by sending the element <MATH_0005>\nof <MATH_0006> to <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d565a400c22a016665b1178b3e2a017abde89a107024196a7eac2bbfcd750be6", "unit_id": "tag:001P:proof"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{C}\\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$h_U$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-representable-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8617b68941d99590a40b9b2ff3bd6990de79f088a23bf90719c80a0898033314", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2ffdb6797ca5bf69a8fa86fe0a6e2342f58513cb742dec83023ff882a9a57982", "source_text": "A contravariant functor <MATH_0001> is said\nto be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it is isomorphic to the functor of\npoints <MATH_0002> for some object <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aefd1fdc2503c4859327faef7fbcd25ab1c66091fd4351d0e33c48f1923dc5fc", "unit_id": "tag:001Q:statement"}
